with these horse racing tips today.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Every selection below shows the most popular pick for that race, so click through to any runner to see all the tips, the reasoning behind them and the tipsters backing each horse. For today's free betting tips across other sports, head over to the main daily \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips\">betting tips page\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>",pageType:"Categories or Leagues",megaMenu:[{title:"All Sports",url:"/betting-tips",type:"sport"},{title:"Horse Racing",url:"/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/2",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Horse_Racing",rank:1,items:void 0,sportId:2,hasItems:true},{title:"Football",url:"/betting-tips/Football/1",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Football",rank:2,items:void 0,sportId:1,hasItems:true},{title:"Tennis",url:"/betting-tips/Tennis/3",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Tennis",rank:3,items:void 0,sportId:3,hasItems:true},{title:"Cricket",url:"/betting-tips/Cricket/7",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Cricket",rank:4,items:void 0,sportId:7,hasItems:true},{title:"Greyhounds",url:"/betting-tips/Greyhounds/28",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Greyhounds",rank:6,sportId:28,items:void 0,hasItems:void 0},{title:"Basketball",url:"/betting-tips/Basketball/4",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Basketball",rank:7,items:void 0,sportId:4,hasItems:true},{title:"American Football",url:"/betting-tips/American_Football/11",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-American_Football",rank:7,items:void 0,sportId:11,hasItems:true},{title:"Baseball",url:"/betting-tips/Baseball/12",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Baseball",rank:7,items:void 0,sportId:12,hasItems:true},{title:"Ice Hockey",url:"/betting-tips/Ice_Hockey/13",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Ice_Hockey",rank:7,items:void 0,sportId:13,hasItems:true},{title:"Golf",url:"/betting-tips/Golf/5",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Golf",rank:8,items:void 0,sportId:5,hasItems:true},{title:"Boxing",url:"/betting-tips/Boxing/16",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Boxing",rank:9,items:void 0,sportId:16,hasItems:true},{title:"Snooker",url:"/betting-tips/Snooker/8",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Snooker",rank:10,sportId:8,items:void 0,hasItems:void 0},{title:"Motor Racing",url:"/betting-tips/Motor_Racing/14",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Motor_Racing",rank:11,items:void 0,sportId:14,hasItems:true},{title:"Darts",url:"/betting-tips/Darts/15",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Darts",rank:12,items:void 0,sportId:15,hasItems:true},{title:"Rugby Union",url:"/betting-tips/Rugby_Union/9",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Rugby_Union",rank:14,items:void 0,sportId:9,hasItems:true},{title:"Rugby League",url:"/betting-tips/Rugby_League/10",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Rugby_League",rank:14,items:void 0,sportId:10,hasItems:true},{title:"Gaelic Football",url:"/betting-tips/Gaelic_Football/25",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Gaelic_Football",rank:20,items:void 0,sportId:25,hasItems:true},{title:"Hurling",url:"/betting-tips/Hurling/26",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Hurling",rank:20,items:void 0,sportId:26,hasItems:true},{title:"Handball",url:"/betting-tips/Handball/20",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Handball",rank:49,items:void 0,sportId:20,hasItems:true},{title:"Volleyball",url:"/betting-tips/Volleyball/21",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Volleyball",rank:50,items:void 0,sportId:21,hasItems:true}],breadcrumbs:[{title:"Horse Racing",url:"/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/2",type:"sport",breadcrumbIdx:"betting-tips-Horse_Racing",parentSport:2}],availableAds:new Map([["tips-header",void 0],["site-takeover",void 0]]),search:null,bettingTipsParams:{sportId:"2",sportName:"Horse_Racing",categoryName:null,leagueName:null,eventName:null,limit:20,tipsApiUrl:"https://tipsb.olbg.info/sports/Horse_Racing/top_tips?source=&paginate=1-100&include_recommendations=1&include_expired=1&ti=bc08d704c435d69fec4f7d5c0de15f261792702811817:ouk:google-chrome:unknown:131.0&api_key=S6H8MM3KN52Q8KN8&bookie_name=_best_&client_type=desktop_website"},tiParam:"bc08d704c435d69fec4f7d5c0de15f261792702811817:ouk:google-chrome:unknown:131.0",deviceType:"D",from:null,tkbSettings:{take_over_banners:"3",take_over_banners_position_fixed:"1",start:"2023-09-11 13:38:19",end:"2026-10-31 08:37:03",_cachedAt:"2026-10-22T21:00:08.196Z",_cacheKey:"takeover-banners-settings",_flushedByIp:"10.182.96.9"},zones:[{slug:"in-events-list",location_id:"L1"}],isHotTips:false,content:{content:{sections:[{title:"How to Find Today's Best Horse Racing Tips",sections_content:"\u003Cp>On this page, our horse racing tipsters share their best free horse racing tips for today's racing around the world. Each race shows the most-tipped runner at a glance, so you can quickly see where the OLBG community is most confident.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Click through on any runner to see the full picture: every tip on that race, the tipsters backing each horse, and the reasoning behind their selections. The win-tips percentage shows how strongly a runner is fancied, the crown highlights how many expert tipsters are on board, and the star value rating compares a selection's popularity against its odds.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Read on to learn how our tipsters find their selections, how to filter the racing tips today by country or bet type, and where to find the latest in-form trainer, jockey and course statistics.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Horse Racing Tips By Bet Type",sections_content:"\u003Cp>Some of our users like to place certain types of bets on horse racing. For example, some like each-way betting, others may only bet on the live ITV races, and some prefer to back the most popular Naps. We have dedicated horse racing tips pages for each of these bet types.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>The Nap of The Day Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>A tipster's best bet of the day can be designated as their Nap. This is one of the most popular pages on the site, with some users liking to bet on a tipster's bet of the day or follow the most popular racing tips today from the OLBG tipsters' best bets. Here we have today's \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/naps_tips/2\">Nap of the Day tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Today's Best Each-Way Horse Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Most horse racing tips are win tips, so we recommend a bet on the horse to win the race. If, however, a tipster thinks a horse is a good bet to either win or place, they will recommend an each-way bet. Many of our users like to place each-way bets as they are more likely to get a return. Some prefer to bet at longer odds and are happy to get a return if their horse comes close to winning. If that is how you like to bet, take a look at our dedicated page for \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/ews_tips/2\">today's best each-way racing tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>ITV Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Some users want to jump straight to our tips for ITV races, so we have a page for those too. If you just want to settle down for the afternoon watching the ITV racing and betting on those races only, we have a dedicated \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/itv_racing/2\">ITV racing tips page\u003C/a> for your convenience.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Tips for the Next Horse Races\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>If you are following all of today's racing, perhaps on the racing channels or in the betting shop, you may want a page that updates with the free horse racing tips for the next races coming up only. For your convenience, we have built exactly that, so you can simply see the best bets on the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/next_races/2\">next horse races\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Today's Horse Racing Acca Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>If you like to place acca bets with multiple selections, take a look at our automated \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/accumulator-tips\">accumulator tips\u003C/a> for horse racing. These take the form of a daily racing double, a four-fold and an each-way Lucky 15, and are usually all available just after 11 am (GMT). The daily acca selections are the horse racing tips from the best profit-performing expert tipsters on OLBG, so they represent the best racing tips today. On the Accumulator Tips page, you can select \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/my-acca\">My Acca\u003C/a> and build your own horse racing acca bets by choosing the number of horse racing tips you wish to include. Again, these will be the best predictions available at the time of request from the expert horse racing tipsters.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Tomorrow's Horse Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Free horse racing tips for tomorrow's racing will be online this afternoon. Our tipsters add their predictions at any time from when the runners are available, right through to around 15 minutes before the race start time.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Horse Racing Tips By Country",sections_content:"\u003Cp>At OLBG, we provide free racing predictions from 10 countries and over 150 courses. If you want the best racing bets from a specific country, click through to the dedicated page.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>UK Horse Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>The UK has arguably the highest quality horse racing in the world. Many of our UK users like to bet on UK racing only, so you can filter out tips from the rest of the world and see a page with just \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/2\">UK Horse Racing Tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Irish Horse Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Irish racing enthusiasts will argue that point, especially when it comes to National Hunt racing. Prize money at Punchestown is now so good that some top stables keep their horses for that meeting rather than send them to the UK for the Aintree Grand National meeting. If you just want to see racing tips today from Ireland, go to our page dedicated to \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/2\">Irish Horse Racing Tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>US Horse Racing Picks\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>After the racing has finished in the UK, the TV channels and bookie screens will often switch to US racing, which has become increasingly popular. So if you want to check out this evening's free horse racing tips for the USA, we have them all in one place on our \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/US/2\">US Horse Racing Picks\u003C/a> page.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Australian Horse Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Another benefit of the time difference for UK racing enthusiasts is Australian horse racing. Follow this link to see the \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/AUS/2\">Australian Horse Racing Tips\u003C/a> from OLBG's horse racing tipsters, covering weekly meetings plus the big events, for example Melbourne Cup tips for Flemington.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>French Horse Racing Selections\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>French racing has some high-quality races, particularly on the Flat and for younger National Hunt horses. In the UK, we see many top horses from French racing bought up by leading yards for a career here. Our tipsters are on the lookout for these as they study French racing and provide you with daily \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/FR/2\">French Horse Racing Tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Hong Kong Horse Racing Predictions\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>The prize money is huge, and the big meetings at Happy Valley and Sha Tin are very popular with horse racing fans across the globe, and in particular the UK, where the races are often scheduled before domestic racing gets underway. Well-known UK jockeys frequently spend time in Hong Kong, and our horse racing tipsters keep track of those heading over for the big rides in their \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/HK/2\">Hong Kong Racing Tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Canadian Horse Racing Tips\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Canada boasts some racetracks of its own, like Woodbine, which are often grouped in with US courses. We don't do that! Canadian racing has its own dedicated page here – \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/CA/2\">Canadian Horse Racing Tips\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>UAE/Dubai Horse Racing Predictions\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>We all know about the huge sums spent on racehorses in the Middle East, which makes our \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UAE/2\">Dubai Racing Tips\u003C/a> a well-visited page. The prize money on offer there can be staggering, and the top meetings attract plenty of interest for Dubai World Cup tips, as do the regular Meydan meetings.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Why and How to Use Free Horse Racing Predictions from OLBG",sections_content:"\u003Cp>There are many ways to find a selection using the horse racing tips today at OLBG. The following are all important aspects of the betting strategies we as punters use when looking for horse racing selections to back.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Whether it's following the most popular horse racing tips today by the number of picks from the OLBG horse racing experts, or looking for \"value\" – an underpriced favourite or an outsider that appears to have been overlooked – there's an angle to suit every approach.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Following the highest profit-performing horse racing tipsters over the last twelve months, sticking with current hot-streak tipsters, or searching for the most detailed tip analysis: we cover all of these with the free horse racing tips on OLBG.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>However you use them, remember our horse racing tips are shared for information to help you make your own betting decisions; they're the opinions of the OLBG tipsters, and they are not certainties, so we would always advise that you do your own research rather than following any tip blindly. In the space between the tipsters posting their tips and the race itself, many factors could change, which can affect the tips, such as changing weather and jockey replacements, so always double-check the comments against live situations. Even the most profitable tipsters on OLBG have losing runs, and their past results are no guarantee of future returns. Please gamble responsibly by setting yourself a budget, and only ever staking what you can afford to lose. If gambling is affecting you or someone close to you, support is available through&nbsp;\u003Ca href=\"https://www.gambleaware.org\">GambleAware\u003C/a> and&nbsp;\u003Ca href=\"https://www.gamcare.org.uk\">GamCare\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Most Popular Horse Racing Tips\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Value Horse Racing Tips\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Most Profitable Tipsters\u003C/li>\u003Cli>In-Form Tipsters\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Expert Tipsters\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Detailed Reasoning For Horse Racing Tips Today\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003Cp>Here we explain in more detail how you can analyse the free horse racing tips provided by OLBG's expert racing tipsters.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Most Popular Horse Racing Tips at OLBG\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>This page lists today's most popular horse racing tips from the community of tipsters at OLBG. If you click on the Tips &amp; Comments tab in the menu above, the tips will be sorted by volume of win tips, so you can look down the list in order of popularity.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>These popular horse racing tips are also known as hot tips. We display the number of tips for each selection, along with the percentage of all tips on that race which have gone on that selection.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Value Horse Racing Tips from OLBG\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Our easy star guide lets you compare popular horse racing tips today with their odds, helping you put together a strategy to get the best value on the best tip for each race. One to five stars are allocated based on a comparison between the percentage of winning tips given to a horse and the odds of the selection.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If a horse is more popular than its odds suggest, it's an indication that it is well-fancied by the OLBG tipsters compared to its chances according to the betting odds. Many of our users treat this as a value bet indicator. Click Value Rating in the menu to sort today's free horse racing tips by star rating, five stars being the best.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Today's Horse Racing Tips from the Most Profitable Tipsters\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>OLBG is a community of knowledgeable sports bettors. Partly due to our long-running sponsorship of the OLBG Road to Cheltenham, we have built up a particularly strong group of expert horse racing tipsters.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Our best horse racing tipsters are consistently profitable, as shown by the Monthly Profit Trend figures alongside their tips. You can also see their level stakes profit (based on horse racing tips only) for the last 12 months, plus their strike rate (also based on horse racing tips only).\u003C/p>\u003Cp>On this page, the horse racing tipsters with the best profit performance are displayed most prominently. To analyse the most profitable horse racing tipsters in more detail, head to our \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/best-tipsters/Horse_Racing/2\">best horse racing tipsters\u003C/a> page, also covered in a later section on this page.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Tips from In-Form Tipsters\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Some of our users like to follow tipsters on a good run. We provide data such as this month's strike rate, this month's profitability, or a tipster with several days in profit in a row.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Again, you can analyse this information on our \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/best-tipsters/Horse_Racing/2\">best horse racing tipsters\u003C/a> page, or dig into the stats here by choosing a race and then a tipster to see their profile.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Predictions from Expert Tipsters\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Expert is a term reserved for the tipsters at OLBG with the very best records. These are profitable, consistent tipsters who meet strict criteria. The number of expert racing tipsters tipping a selection is indicated by the crown symbol.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If you see this symbol, you may want to look in more detail at what the expert has to say about the selection and why they are tipping that horse today.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Just click through on the name of the horse, then look for the tipster or tipsters with a crown beside their name. There you can see the tipster's record and understand why we have labelled them an expert.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Detailed Reasoning for Horse Racing Tips Today\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Most other sites provide tips with little reasoning as to why a tipster is recommending a bet, which gives people little confidence in following them. We find our users want to understand why a recommendation has been made.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>This supports learning, a core principle of OLBG, which exists to help sports bettors learn from each other. A well-reasoned argument for backing a racing tip is what many like to see, and our site is well moderated by an in-house team as well as volunteer members.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Tip comments can be rated, and over time we get to know the tipsters who research the tips they make. This validates the time and effort that many of our top horse racing tipsters dedicate to supplying their free horse racing tips.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Not only does this save you a lot of time as you research the best bets for yourself, but it also helps you understand how the best racing tipsters find their horse racing tips. Reading these comments regularly will give you great insight into their selection strategy.\u003C/p>"},{title:"How Do OLBG Tipsters Pick a Winning Horse?",sections_content:"\u003Cp>There are numerous variables to consider when picking a winning horse, and OLBG's horse racing tipsters each have their own strategies and methods for selecting their daily horse racing tips. These may include specialising in specific types of races, assessing the previous form of the day's runners, analysing race trends for the big meetings, following favourite or in-form jockeys and trainers, focusing on runners at \"value\" odds, taking a systematic approach, and much more.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Those are just a handful of methods for selecting horse racing tips. In most cases, a tipster will use a combination of these, plus others, in an elimination process to build a shortlist for any given race. It may then come down to the respective odds of each runner on that shortlist before they place their free horse racing tips.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Here is a brief description of the betting strategies mentioned:\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Specialising in Specific Types of Horse Races\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Most successful tipsters keep a detailed record of their selections, which shows their profit (or losses) and helps highlight the types of races where they excel and flag those where their record is weaker. By specific races, we mean the various categories such as Flat races, handicaps, maidens (for horses yet to win), novice races, sprints (5 and 6 furlongs), chases and hurdles. Knowing this can help a tipster narrow their focus to the races that best suit them.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Assessing Previous Horse Racing Form\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Tipsters analyse the previous performances (form) of today's runners using their skill and expertise. This involves evaluating each runner's recent and career form, comparing their optimum conditions (ground, distance, class, and so on) against today's race, and creating a shortlist of those they feel hold the best claims. Racing's trade paper, the Racing Post, is a popular resource for extensive form study, along with other free-to-use sources such as the Sporting Life and At The Races websites, where the day's racecards and form can be viewed. Form is a highly important factor, but just one of many to weigh up. For a more in-depth look, check out our \u003Ca href=\"/school/reading-horse-racing-form\">How to Read Horse Racing Form\u003C/a> article in the Betting School section.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Following Favourite or In-Form Trainers &amp; Jockeys\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Following trainers or jockeys blindly can be risky; however, tipsters build up knowledge of specific traits, such as a trainer who does well with runners at a particular racecourse or in a race they've won on numerous occasions (\"horses for courses\"). Studying trainer and jockey performance statistics at each course unearths pointers and is another important cog when analysing a race, and can be the difference when settling on a shortlist. Stables enjoying a \"purple patch\" of winners are also a key factor, and horses that have previously been below par may suddenly be at their peak and ready to perform above expectations.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Focusing on \"Value\" Odds\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Most tipsters will have an idea of what they consider \"value\" odds on their daily horse racing tips. Value can apply to a race favourite available at a bigger price than expected, or to a longer-priced selection that still looks better than anticipated. Many experienced tipsters are skilled at setting the odds for a race themselves (much like a bookmaker); this is known as compiling a \"tissue\", and it helps them decide whether their selection is available to back at a value price. The odds on offer are, in most cases, the deciding factor when a tipster has more than one runner on their shortlist. Some tipsters focus solely on a specific odds range, concentrating on mid-priced runners rather than short-priced favourites. They may encounter slightly longer losing runs, as these runners win less often than favourites at much shorter odds; however, the returns are consistently more rewarding. Their strike rate may be lower as a result, but their return on investment (ROI) – shown as a percentage and calculated by dividing profit by total stake – should be healthy. For a more detailed look at finding value, take some time to read our \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/school/value-betting\">Value Betting\u003C/a> article, which looks at making your betting more profitable.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>A Systematic Approach\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Traditional form-book purists may scoff at this method; however, it appeals to many tipsters, particularly those who prefer not to have their head buried in the form book for hours on end. Horse racing betting systems are generally created by a computer analysing thousands of previous results over a defined period, with the tipster then applying a range of filters (form, course, trainer, jockey, and so on) to crunch the data into a set of stats (profit/loss, number of selections, and the like) and see whether there's a profitable betting angle. You'll find numerous articles on the systematic approach, like \u003Ca href=\"/blogs/the-best-horse-racing-betting-system-ever-can-work\">The Best Horse Racing Betting System Ever, Can it Work?\u003C/a>, in our \u003Ca href=\"/blogs\">Insights section\u003C/a> on OLBG.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Horse Racing Trends Analysis\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Many tipsters like this approach, especially for the prestigious races in the UK and around the world. For example, if a high number of previous Grand National winners had run in a certain number of chases, won over three miles or further, worn no headgear, or carried below a certain weight, that can help build a shortlist of the most likely winners – a useful starting point before further analysis such as form study and stable form. Of course, just because something has happened before doesn't mean it will happen again, but strong trend pointers are worth considering. We have an extensive section of \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/blogs/category/horse-racing\">Horse Racing Trends Blogs\u003C/a> on OLBG, compiled by \u003Ca href=\"/meet-the-experts/andy-powell\">Andy Powell\u003C/a>, covering all the major races around the world plus weekly meetings in the UK and Ireland. Be sure to check them out before betting on your horse racing tips today.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Who Gives the Best Horse Racing Tips?",sections_content:"\u003Cp>OLBG has an army of knowledgeable horse racing tipsters; over 300 compete in the monthly horse racing tipster competitions, so there are plenty to choose from when it comes to finding tipsters who give the best free horse racing tips.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>We outlined in an earlier section the various criteria our users consider when choosing which horse racing tips and tipsters to follow – value picks, most popular picks, best-profit tipsters, current-form tipsters, and so on. All the statistics relevant to these areas are freely available alongside the racing tips today, helping you build a picture of the type of tipster that best suits your style of betting, whether that's favourites (regular winners, generally at shorter prices) or longshots (bigger prices, but often at a lower strike rate).\u003C/p>\u003Cp>\"Best\" can be subjective when it comes to tipping strategy, analysis and the like, so we give you all the information to help you decide which tipsters give the best horse racing tips. Profit performance, however, isn't subjective: a tipster's profit figures are proven and verified over the last 12 months, so the tipsters with the highest profit are those that attract the most demand.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>The Best Horse Racing Tipsters at OLBG\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Our \u003Ca href=\"/best-tipsters/Horse_Racing/2\">best horse racing tipsters\u003C/a> page shows you the most profitable racing tipsters over the last 12 months according to their Level Stakes Profit. Their profitable months help you gauge consistently good tipping, alongside their current month's profit and strike rate over the last 12 months. You'll also see their best day's and month's profit within the last year, and their worst day's and month's loss, figures that may help you decide on a starting bank for your horse racing bets.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>If you like a tipster's stats, click the link in the final column to see their horse racing tips today. Our best horse racing tipsters also add reasoning with their tips, so you can see why each selection is recommended and get an insight into their strategy. Following a specific tipster and digesting their tip analysis over time helps you understand their selection process.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>You can also follow your favourite horse racing tipsters on the \u003Ca href=\"/feed\">OLBG feed\u003C/a>. Once you find a tipster you like, click to follow them, and their tips will start showing in your feed. Two of OLBG's long-standing horse racing tipsters, \u003Ca href=\"/best-tipsters/Horse_Racing/2/114000\">The Prophet\u003C/a> and \u003Ca href=\"/best-tipsters/Horse_Racing/2/375134\">Benaldo1981\u003C/a>, have over 37,000 followers on the OLBG app.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Free Horse Racing Tips at OLBG",sections_content:"\u003Ch3>Do I Need to Pay for Good Horse Racing Tips?\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>We advise against paying for horse racing tips for several reasons. The most important is that there are so many knowledgeable and consistently profitable tipsters here at \u003Cstrong>OLBG who provide free horse racing tips\u003C/strong> that we don't believe you need to risk paying for tips from individuals unknown to you, or from tipping services that may lock you into a subscription for longer than you'd want should you have a change of heart after a bad run of results. OLBG horse racing tipsters compete for generous prize money every month, so they do not need to sell their horse racing tips.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Why Do \"Tipsters\" Sell Tips?\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>There are many reasons a tipster might sell horse racing tips. It may be an additional income that supports their own betting expenses. They may not be able to place bets on their own selections because bookmakers have restricted their staking as a result of previous betting activity. Some tipping services may even require you to place cash bets on their behalf in exchange for daily horse racing tips. There's also the question of whether the selections are genuinely well-researched, and whether the tipping service can substantiate its past profit performance by proofing to a third party.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>In conclusion, OLBG is the best place to come for daily \u003Cstrong>free\u003C/strong> horse racing tips: our tipsters' betting performance stats are available to view alongside their detailed tip analysis, so you always know why they've made a selection.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>As well as our community tipsters, you can also receive free horse racing tips from \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/sam-turner\">Sam Turner\u003C/a>, a five-time Press Challenge champion tipster who shares his selections through a weekly OLBG newsletter that's free to sign up for. His page shows his past selections and running profit and loss record on OLBG, so you can see how he's performing before subscribing – another way to get expert racing tips at no cost, straight to your inbox.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Do You Recommend Horse Racing Predictions from Other Sites?\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>The Racing Post's Tom Segal, known as \"Pricewise\", has built a reputation for finding value selections, in most cases to beat the race favourite. The difficulty that comes with his following is that the bookies react accordingly and shorten the odds once his daily horse racing tips are published.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>Some media outlets provide horse racing tips for free via knowledgeable racing journalists, such as Templegate's tips in The Sun. The difficulty these tipsters face is that they are often required to put up a tip in every race on the card. Tipsters at OLBG can be more selective, tipping in just one or two races a day, or choosing not to tip at all if they don't find any good bets – exactly how it should be.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>So it's best to stick with OLBG tipsters, where we show you their tip history, strike rate, consistency via recent profitable months, overall profitability and return on investment. They have to back their tips up with sound reasoning too, so you can understand why they're recommending each bet, and then choose which tips and tipsters you want to follow.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Top Horse Racing Courses for Winning Favourites",sections_content:"\u003Cp>Favourites don't win everywhere at the same rate, so knowing which courses see the most winning favourites can shape your horse racing tips. Below are the top five UK and Irish courses for outright favourites over the past year, updated monthly.\u003C/p>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Course\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Code\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Favourite win rate\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Lingfield/2\">Lingfield\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Flat\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>53.01%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/Killarney/2\">Killarney\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>NH\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>51.06%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Lingfield/2\">Lingfield\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>NH\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>50.00%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/Tipperary/2\">Tipperary\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>NH\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>50.00%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Bangor_on_Dee/2\">Bangor\u003C/a>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>NH\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>47.95%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Ch3>Lingfield – Flat (Turf)\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>With a strong track record, \u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Lingfield/2\">Lingfield\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> leads the list, boasting a 53.01% win rate for outright favourites over the past year. Out of 83 races, 44 resulted in victories for the favourites. Those favourites came from a total of 88 at Lingfield, which means a total of 94% of the races at this track featured an outright favourite.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>During that time, the most successful trainer was \u003Cstrong>Sir Mark Prescott\u003C/strong>, who notched up a total of 3 winners from their 4 runners who were outright favourites at Lingfield. Regarding jockeys, the most successful was \u003Cstrong>Harry Vigors\u003C/strong>; from a total of 3 rides on outright favourites at Lingfield, they managed to pick up 3 winners.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Killarney – Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/Killarney/2\">Killarney\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> holds the second spot with a 51.06% success rate for favourites, having seen 24 winners from 47 races in the past year. With a total of 53 races at Killarney during that period, a total of 89% of races featured an outright favourite at this track.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>W P Mullins\u003C/strong> proved to be the most successful trainer at Killarney, securing 6 wins from 9 outright favourites. Among jockeys, \u003Cstrong>Darragh O'Keeffe\u003C/strong> was the standout, with 4 victories from 5 rides on outright favourites at the same venue.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Lingfield – Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Third up is \u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Lingfield/2\">Lingfield\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> with a 50.00% win rate for favourites over 44 races, yielding 22 winners. There were a total of 45 races at Lingfield over the past year, and from those, a total of 98% of races featured an outright favourite.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>The Jockey who has ridden the most outright favourite winners at Lingfield is \u003Cstrong>Sean P Bowen\u003C/strong>, who has ridden 3 winners over the past year from a total of 6 rides.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Tipperary – Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Over the past year, there have been a total of 12 races at \u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/Tipperary/2\">Tipperary\u003C/a>\u003C/strong>. All of the races (12) featured an outright favourite, and from those races, a total of 6 of the favourites went on to win, which gives the outright favourites a 50.00% strike rate at Tipperary over the past year.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>One trainer to watch out for at Tipperary when it comes to outright favourites is \u003Cstrong>W P Mullins\u003C/strong>. Over the past year, they have had 3 winners from a total of 3 runners and have led the way for outright favourites. When it comes to who is in the saddle, then watch out for \u003Cstrong>P Townend\u003C/strong>, they have ridden 3 outright favourites at Tipperary, of which 3 have gone on to win.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Bangor – Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Rounding off the top five courses for outright favourites is \u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Bangor_on_Dee/2\">Bangor\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> with a 47.95% win rate for favourites, with 35 winners from 73 races. With a total of 80 races at Bangor during that period, that means that 91% of races featured an outright favourite at this track.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>We have mentioned the outright favourite statistics for Bangor, but which trainer and jockey top the lists for those? \u003Cstrong>Daniel Skelton\u003C/strong> is the top trainer with 7 winners from their 9 runners. Whilst, in terms of those in the saddle, with 7 winners from 9 rides on outright favourites at Bangor, it is \u003Cstrong>Harry Skelton\u003C/strong> who tops the list.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Hot Trainers - Top In-Form Horse Racing Trainers",sections_content:"\u003Cp>Following the trainers in form can be a useful angle when weighing up your horse racing tips. Below are the top five horse racing trainers by strike rate over the previous month, refreshed at the start of each month.\u003C/p>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Trainer\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Category\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Strike rate\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Patrick Neville\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Jumps\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>58.33%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Charlie Appleby\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Non-Handicaps on the Flat (Turf)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>57.14%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>K R Burke\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Novices' on the Flat (Turf)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>43.75%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>J H M Gosden\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>All-Weather\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>43.75%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Jonjo and AJ O'Neill\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Handicap Chases over Jumps\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>40.00%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Ch3>Patrick Neville – Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Ranked at the top of the in-form trainers list heading into October is \u003Cstrong>Patrick Neville\u003C/strong>, who in September saw 58% of their runners go on to be successful; that was 7 from a total of 12 runners in jump races. Of those runners, their biggest winner of the month was \u003Cstrong>Upfordebate\u003C/strong>, who won on Thursday, 24th of September at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Perth/2\">Perth\u003C/a> under the guidance of Brian Hughes at a starting price of 8/1. For their winners, it was \u003Cstrong>Brian Hughes\u003C/strong> who delivered the most; they produced all of Patrick Neville winners in jump races during September.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Charlie Appleby – Non-Handicaps on the Flat (Turf)\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Second on the list, with a strike rate of 57% for their runners in Non-Handicaps on the flat (turf) during September, is \u003Cstrong>Charlie Appleby\u003C/strong>. They head into October after sending out a total of 21 last month in Non-Handicaps on the flat (turf), which returned 12 winners, the highlight of those winners being \u003Cstrong>Arabian Crown\u003C/strong>, who James Doyle rode to success at an SP of 11/1 at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/Leopardstown/2\">Leopardstown\u003C/a> on Saturday, 12th of September. Looking at who rode Charlie Appleby's mentioned runners to success, then \u003Cstrong>William Buick\u003C/strong> was the standout jockey, winning on 83% of those winners.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>K R Burke – Novices' on the Flat (Turf)\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Rounding out the top three on the in-form trainers is \u003Cstrong>K R Burke\u003C/strong> for their runners in Novices' on the flat (turf), which produced a 44% strike rate during September. Those winners came as a result of 7 winners from 16 runners, with \u003Cstrong>Lady Foxtrot\u003C/strong> being their best result, which won at an SP of 14/1 at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Carlisle/2\">Carlisle\u003C/a> on Wednesday, 9th of September.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>J H M Gosden – All-Weather\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>J H M Gosden\u003C/strong> is next on the list for the most in-form trainer during September, with a strike rate of 44% for their runners on the All-Weather, who managed to produce 7 winners during the month from 16 runners. The standout runner was \u003Cstrong>Exposure\u003C/strong>, who won at an SP of 15/2 at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Kempton/2\">Kempton\u003C/a> on Saturday, 5th of September, with B D L Sayette in the saddle. Looking at the winners J H M Gosden had during September in the mentioned race type, one thing which stands out is that \u003Cstrong>Robert Havlin\u003C/strong> was in the saddle for 57% of those winners, so watch out when they are booked.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Jonjo and AJ O'Neill – Handicap Chases over Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Finally, the top five is finished off with \u003Cstrong>Jonjo and AJ O'Neill\u003C/strong> for their runners in Handicap Chases over jumps, who returned a strike rate of 40% in September, which was made up of 4 winners from 10 runners. Their biggest winner in September was \u003Cstrong>Mt Fugi Park\u003C/strong>, who won at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Uttoxeter/2\">Uttoxeter\u003C/a> on Tuesday, 15th of September at an SP of 13/2.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Hot Jockeys - Top In-Form Horse Racing Jockeys",sections_content:"\u003Cp>Just as with trainers, spotting the jockeys in form can help shape your horse racing tips. Below are the top five horse racing jockeys by strike rate over the previous month, refreshed at the start of each month.\u003C/p>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Jockey\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Category\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Strike rate\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>James C Bowen\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Handicap Chases over Jumps\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>63.64%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Mr P W Mullins\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Jumps\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>54.55%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>David Allan\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Handicap Nurseries on the Flat (Turf)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>50.00%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Connor Beasley\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Handicaps on the All-Weather\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>45.45%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Brendan Powell\u003C/strong>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Handicap Hurdles over Jumps\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>40.00%\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Ch3>James C Bowen – Handicap Chases over Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>The top jockey coming into October is \u003Cstrong>James C Bowen\u003C/strong>, who won on 64% of his rides in September in Handicap Chases over jumps. That strike rate came from a total of 7 winners from a total of 11 rides; the pick of those winners was on Friday, 4th of September, when \u003Cstrong>Limerick Leader\u003C/strong>, trained by Nick Scholfield, went on to success at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Bangor_on_Dee/2\">Bangor\u003C/a> at an SP of 17/2.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Mr P W Mullins – Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Second on the most in-form jockeys' list with a strike rate of 55% in September is \u003Cstrong>Mr P W Mullins\u003C/strong>, who notched up 6 winners from their 11 rides for September in jump races. Looking over their winners for September, the standout at odds of 12/1 was \u003Cstrong>Double Helix\u003C/strong>, trained by Charles Weld, which won at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/IE/Navan/2\">Navan\u003C/a> on Saturday, 19th of September. When teaming up with \u003Cstrong>W P Mullins\u003C/strong> in October, then do take note of the mentioned runners; they supplied Mr P W Mullins with 67% of their winners in September.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>David Allan – Handicap Nurseries on the Flat (Turf)\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Next up is \u003Cstrong>David Allan\u003C/strong> in Handicap Nurseries on the flat (turf), for which in September they produced 5 winners from 10 rides, which was a 50% strike rate. The pick of their winners was at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Ripon/2\">Ripon\u003C/a> on Tuesday, 1st of September, when they rode \u003Cstrong>May Bee In Profit\u003C/strong> to success at odds of 9/1 for T D Easterby. If you are planning on following David Allan's rides in October, then take note when he is booked by \u003Cstrong>T D Easterby,\u003C/strong> as all of their winners in September were when teaming up with that yard.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Connor Beasley – Handicaps on the All-Weather\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Connor Beasley\u003C/strong> had a 45% strike rate in September in Handicaps on the all-weather, which puts them fourth on the in-form jockeys list! That came from 5 winners from their 11 rides, with the pick of those being the M Dods runner \u003Cstrong>Tatterstall\u003C/strong>, who won at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Lingfield/2\">Lingfield\u003C/a> at an SP of 13/2 on Saturday, 12th of September.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>Brendan Powell – Handicap Hurdles over Jumps\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>Rounding out the top five in-form jockeys is \u003Cstrong>Brendan Powell\u003C/strong>, who in September notched up a total of 4 winners in Handicap Hurdles over jumps from 10 rides, which works out as a 40% strike rate. Going over those winners, the standout was \u003Cstrong>Uncle Remus\u003C/strong>, who at 22/1 won at \u003Ca href=\"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/UK/Uttoxeter/2\">Uttoxeter\u003C/a> on Tuesday, 15th of September, for Miss H C Knight. The team of \u003Cstrong>Miss H C Knight\u003C/strong> and Brendan Powell worked well in September, with \u003Cstrong>Miss H C Knight\u003C/strong> supplying Brendan Powell with 75% of his winners in Handicap Hurdles over jumps.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Top 10 Draw Biases",sections_content:"\u003Cp>The draw – the stall a horse starts from – can have a real bearing on its chances at certain courses and trips, which is why many tipsters factor it into their horse racing tips. Below are the top 10 stalls based on results over the past year, refreshed at the start of each month.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>We look at each stall at each course over each trip, and these are the top ten based on those that have produced five or more winners, ordered by the best LSP (Level Stakes Profit).\u003C/p>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Info\u003C/th>\u003Cth>LSP\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Newcastle (AW)\u003C/strong> - Stall 11 over 7f (6 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+109.75\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Newcastle (AW)\u003C/strong> - Stall 5 over 6f (20 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+96.86\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Doncaster\u003C/strong> - Stall 5 over 6f (6 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+72.40\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Yarmouth\u003C/strong> - Stall 3 over 6f (8 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+70.58\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Chelmsford City (AW)\u003C/strong> - Stall 8 over 6f (5 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+69.97\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Beverley\u003C/strong> - Stall 2 over 5f (10 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+64.10\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Dundalk (AW)\u003C/strong> - Stall 6 over 1m (10 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+62.85\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Carlisle\u003C/strong> - Stall 2 over 6f (6 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+62.33\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Ayr\u003C/strong> - Stall 6 over 6f (5 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+62.08\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Newcastle (AW)\u003C/strong> - Stall 8 over 1m2f (8 winners)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>+61.88\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Cp class=\"text-muted\">The favourite, trainer, jockey and draw bias statistics included in the content above include all races in the UK and Ireland between Wednesday 1st of October 2025 and Wednesday 30th of September 2026. These statistics have all been sourced from \u003Ca href=\"https://www.horseracebase.com\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">HorseRaceBase\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>"},{title:"More Horse Racing Tips & Resources To Place a Bet",sections_content:"\u003Ch3>Where Can I Get More Detailed Horse Racing Forecasts?\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>You can read comments for every horse in every race via the tips on this page or in the OLBG app. For even more in-depth research, we also have detailed horse racing tips blogs written by our horse racing betting specialists, as mentioned in the previous section. These cover subjects such as key race statistics and big-race trends, for example, the \u003Ca href=\"/blogs/cheltenham-gold-cup\">Cheltenham Gold Cup trends\u003C/a>, along with race-by-race guides for the main UK races, in-form trainers, ante-post horse racing tips and other analysis.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>There are also many specific articles written for the key races, especially the racing festivals, which include:\u003C/p>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Cheltenham\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Aintree\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Royal Ascot\u003C/li>\u003Cli>Glorious Goodwood\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003Cp>We've also put together a guide to the \u003Ca href=\"/bookmakers/articles/best-horse-racing\">best horse racing betting sites\u003C/a>. Check that out to see whether you're betting with the \u003Ca href=\"/bookmakers.php\">best betting site\u003C/a> for your horse racing bets. Around the top racing festivals especially, the bookies offer some very generous welcome offers, so be sure to check those out on our \u003Ca href=\"/free.php\">free bets\u003C/a> page.\u003C/p>"},{title:"Horse Racing Prediction Competitions at OLBG",sections_content:"\u003Cp>Every month, more than £1,000 in cash prizes is available from our main horse racing tipster competition, as well as £200 from the daily horse racing Naps competition. We also have separate prizes for the Horse Racing All Tips competition, Irish racing tips and horse racing acca tips. You can join OLBG for free and take part in all the racing tipster competitions.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>You'll need to be good to win these cash prizes, as we have some excellent and consistently profitable horse racing tipsters at OLBG. But don't be put off, as prizes currently reach down to 134th place in the main horse racing tips table.\u003C/p>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Ccaption>Horse Racing Tipster Competitions at OLBG\u003C/caption>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Competition\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Prize Money (monthly)\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Prizes (total)\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Top Prize\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Horse Racing Overall\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£1,000\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>134\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£200\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Horse Racing Naps\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£200\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>27\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£50\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Horse Racing All Tips\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£100\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£25\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Irish Racing\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£100\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£25\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Horse Racing 4-Fold\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£100\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£25\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\u003Cp>To win some of the larger prizes, we do ask members to add reasoning for their tips. Many of our users find this helps their own betting, taking the time to write down why they're making or suggesting a bet. It's also really useful for horse racing tip followers to understand why a bet is being recommended.\u003C/p>\u003Cp>However, you can still add your picks and win smaller prizes if you'd prefer not to provide this information. We used to offer free bets as prizes, but have recently replaced these with cash prizes too.\u003C/p>\u003Ch3>More Horse Racing Tips Competitions at OLBG\u003C/h3>\u003Cp>In addition to the monthly horse racing tips competitions, we also run 'Big Event' tipster competitions covering the major festivals: Cheltenham, the Grand National meeting at Aintree, Royal Ascot and the Breeders' Cup from the USA. Our flagship is the Cheltenham Festival tipster competition, which carries a cash prize fund of £1,500 and over 100 prizes, with the winner receiving £500.\u003C/p>\u003Ctable class=\"table table-bordered table-striped text-left no-branding\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\u003Ccaption>'Big Event' Horse Racing Tipster Competitions at OLBG\u003C/caption>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Competition\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Prize Money\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Prizes (total)\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Top Prize\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Cheltenham\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£1,500\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>105\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£500\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Royal Ascot\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£500\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>18\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£200\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Aintree\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£200\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>13\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£50\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Breeders' Cup\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£100\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>15\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>£25\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>"},{title:"Who Created this Content",sections_content:"\u003Cp>An experienced group of OLBG experts manages our OLBG Community horse racing tips, with over 65 years of combined experience in sports betting. Darren Brett spearheads the content with more than three decades of betting industry knowledge, complemented by the betting strategies devised by Andy Powell, a 20-year-plus veteran. Rounding out the trio is James Banting, whose 20-plus years of experience in betting and as a keen follower and racegoer ensure the tips are in good hands. Together, they collaborate with the invaluable OLBG Tipster community to provide tips that help punters make informed betting decisions.\u003C/p>\u003Cdiv class=\"author-box-component mb-8 p-6 bg-olbg-light-blue rounded-md items-center md:items-start justify-center md:justify-start flex flex-col md:flex-row color-bleu  compact\">\u003Ca class=\"rounded-full flex justify-center items-center overflow-hidden w-24 h-24 mb-6 md:mr-6 border-[6px] border-gray-500 border-opacity-25 image-outside\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/darren-brett\">\u003Cpicture>\u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/ec7/564/649ec7564fbfa346637961.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\"> \u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/ec7/564/649ec7564fbfa346637961.jpeg&amp;w=100&amp;h=100&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(min-width: 1024px)\"> \u003Cimg alt=\"Darren Brett\" src=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/649/ec7/564/649ec7564fbfa346637961.jpeg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" title=\"Darren Brett\" class=\"w-full h-auto\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\">\u003C/picture>\u003C/a> \u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col flex-1 items-center text-center md:items-start md:text-left\">\u003Cp class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Tipster Competition Manager\u003C/p>  \u003Cdiv class=\"mb-2\">Darren has a long history in sports betting and, in particular, horse racing, having even worked as an odds compiler in the past. As OLBG's Tipster Competition Manager, he oversees the monthly racing competitions, and he also runs OLBG's dedicated Grand National Guide. He attends racing whenever his duties allow.\u003C/div> \u003Cp class=\"mb-0 author-box-info\">- \u003Ca class=\"font-bold underline text-olbg-blue-gray hover:text-olbg-orange\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/darren-brett\">Darren Brett\u003C/a>, Content Editor\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"author-box-component mb-8 p-6 bg-olbg-light-blue rounded-md items-center md:items-start justify-center md:justify-start flex flex-col md:flex-row color-bleu  compact\">\u003Ca class=\"rounded-full flex justify-center items-center overflow-hidden w-24 h-24 mb-6 md:mr-6 border-[6px] border-gray-500 border-opacity-25 image-outside\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/james-banting\">\u003Cpicture>\u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/646/cad/0b9/646cad0b934d0036752766.jpg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\"> \u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/646/cad/0b9/646cad0b934d0036752766.jpg&amp;w=100&amp;h=100&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(min-width: 1024px)\"> \u003Cimg alt=\"James Banting\" src=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/646/cad/0b9/646cad0b934d0036752766.jpg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" title=\"James Banting\" class=\"w-full h-auto\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\">\u003C/picture>\u003C/a> \u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col flex-1 items-center text-center md:items-start md:text-left\">\u003Cp class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Horse Racing Specialist\u003C/p>  \u003Cdiv class=\"mb-2\">James Banting brings a wealth of horse racing experience to OLBG, having attended countless race meetings over the years and visited more UK racecourses than anyone else at OLBG. His background working with the Jockey Association gives him a genuine insider's perspective on the industry, and he's a key member of the OLBG Racing team.\u003C/div> \u003Cp class=\"mb-0 author-box-info\">- \u003Ca class=\"font-bold underline text-olbg-blue-gray hover:text-olbg-orange\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/james-banting\">James Banting\u003C/a>, Content Editor\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"author-box-component mb-8 p-6 bg-[#414a5e] text-white rounded-md items-center md:items-start justify-center md:justify-start flex flex-col md:flex-row color-dark  compact\">\u003Ca class=\"rounded-full flex justify-center items-center overflow-hidden w-24 h-24 mb-6 md:mr-6 border-[6px] border-gray-500 border-opacity-25 image-outside\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/andy-powell\">\u003Cpicture>\u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/646/cb8/b22/646cb8b22351f225446960.jpg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\"> \u003Csource srcset=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/646/cb8/b22/646cb8b22351f225446960.jpg&amp;w=100&amp;h=100&amp;zc=1\" media=\"(min-width: 1024px)\"> \u003Cimg alt=\"Andy Powell\" src=\"https://olbgimages.co.uk/image-cache?src=https://olbgimages.co.uk/storage/gallery/october-app/uploads/public/646/cb8/b22/646cb8b22351f225446960.jpg&amp;w=80&amp;h=80&amp;zc=1\" title=\"Andy Powell\" class=\"w-full h-auto\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\">\u003C/picture>\u003C/a> \u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col flex-1 items-center text-center md:items-start md:text-left\">\u003Cp class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Andy the Stats Man\u003C/p>  \u003Cdiv class=\"mb-2\">Andy has an eye for a number — or, in fact, thousands of them — and has built a program that assesses the lifetime form of every horse to produce his own unique ratings. A regular punter and proud Tractor Boy, Andy is a Cheltenham Festival and Aintree Festival-winning owner, and looks after all of OLBG's horse racing trends blogs.\u003C/div> \u003Cp class=\"mb-0 author-box-info\">- \u003Ca class=\"font-bold underline text-olbg-blue-gray hover:text-olbg-orange\" href=\"/meet-the-experts/andy-powell\">Andy Powell\u003C/a>, Content Editor\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>"},{title:"",sections_content:"\u003Cdiv>\u003Cheader class=\"sct-hdr  \">\u003Ch3 class=\"text-2xl\">\u003Ci class=\"text-2xl i-ui-faq text-olbg-orange\">\u003C/i> FAQ\u003C/h3> \u003Cp class=\"mb-2 text-gray-400 tagline\">Horse Racing Betting Tips FAQ\u003C/p>\u003C/header> \u003Cdiv class=\"faq\">\u003Cdiv class=\"flex flex-col gap-0 sm:gap-3 sm:flex-row fq-cnt\">\u003Cul class=\"flex-1 [&amp;&amp;]:p-0 [&amp;&amp;]:m-0 h-rst-ls\">\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"1\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">How do you bet on horse racing online?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Betting on horse racing online is as easy as going into a high-street betting shop, arguably easier, as you don't have to make the trip. You first need to register for an online account with the betting site you want to use. Horse racing is very popular, so it's easy to find in the app: select the race and the horse you want to back, choose your stake, then check the details on your betslip and confirm.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"2\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">What is the best way to bet on horses?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Many expert and professional gamblers will tell you the best way to bet on horse racing is with single bets, on either the win or place markets. Once you combine selections into one bet, the probability of it winning drops, the strike rate falls, and the odds get bigger. While that can lead to bigger wins, it's harder to make a slow, steady profit than by betting singles alone.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"3\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">Can you bet on a horse to lose?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Yes, it's possible to bet on a horse to lose. This was once the reserve of the bookmaker, but betting exchanges let you bet like one, and many sites now offer the option to back a horse not to win. On an exchange, you lay the horse by offering odds to others who want to back it to win, which differs from a standard bookmaker where the question is simply whether the horse will win the race.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"4\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">What types of bets can you make on horses?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Beyond backing a horse to win, there are a huge number of options. From combining two selections into a double to predicting the first two home (known as a forecast or exacta), there are dozens of bet types available on horse racing.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"5\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">How often does the favourite horse win?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>The favourite wins around 30% of races on average. This is a fluid figure that fluctuates with factors such as the course, the time of year and the going. It's worth investigating more specific favourite-winning statistics on racing stats websites, where you may find courses or conditions at which favourites win more or less often than the general 30% figure, and spot a betting angle.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003Cul class=\"flex-1 [&amp;&amp;]:p-0 [&amp;&amp;]:m-0 h-rst-ls\">\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"1\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">What are the best horse racing tips today?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>The best horse racing tips today are the selections receiving the most predictions from OLBG's horse racing tipsters. Free horse racing tips marked with a crown denote the number of experts backing that selection. Experts are OLBG tipsters with high strike rates and current month or 6-month profitability for a particular sport.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"2\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">When will horse racing tips for tomorrow be available?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>The free horse racing tips for tomorrow are available to view now. Tipsters begin placing their selections from the afternoon before race day, and tips are added up to around 15 minutes before the scheduled off. A tipster may add a tip early if they think the available value is good and expect it to shorten.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"3\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">Should I only use free horse racing tips?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>We believe you don't need to pay for selections from subscription services when we have daily free horse racing tips here from OLBG's expert tipsters. Our tipsters compete for generous prize money in our monthly tipster competitions, so they do not need to sell their tips. Each tipster's profit figures covering up to the last 12 months are shown with their racing tips every day, so you can see who's performing well and choose who to follow.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003Cli data-faq-card=\"\" class=\"group p-2 px-3 [&amp;&amp;]:mb-3 hover:bg-[#fff6e8] hover:cursor-pointer list-none bg-white border rounded border-c-border-2 shadow-sm faq-crd\" data-num=\"4\">\u003Ch4 class=\"p-0 m-0\">\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" data-faq-toggle=\"\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"flex items-center w-full p-0 m-0 text text-left bg-transparent border-0 qa-title\">\u003Cspan class=\"flex-1 max-md:!text-md max-md:leading-relaxed max-md:pr-10 md:!text-base\">Do you have Lucky 15 horse racing tips?\u003C/span> \u003Ci class=\"i-ui-dropdown-arrow text-olbg-orange group-[.card-opened]:-rotate-90 text-xs\">\u003C/i>\u003C/button>\u003C/h4> \u003Cdiv class=\"hidden group-[.card-opened]:block pb-0 mt-2 mb-0 answer\">\u003Cp>Yes, we have daily Lucky 15 horse racing tips, which can be found on our \u003Ca href=\"/accumulator-tips\">Accumulator Tips\u003C/a> list. The selections are the most popular each-way horse racing tips today from the best profit-performing tipsters on OLBG. The daily each-way Lucky 15 tips are available from around 10 am (GMT); if you'd rather use the selections in a Lucky 15 win bet, that's fine too. You can also build your own Lucky 15 using our acca tool to pick from the free horse racing tips on OLBG.\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003C/div> \u003Cdiv>\u003Cscript type=\"application/ld+json\">\n        {\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"name\": \"Horse Racing Betting Tips FAQ\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How do you bet on horse racing online?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Betting on horse racing online is as easy as going into a high-street betting shop, arguably easier, as you don't have to make the trip. You first need to register for an online account with the betting site you want to use. Horse racing is very popular, so it's easy to find in the app: select the race and the horse you want to back, choose your stake, then check the details on your betslip and confirm.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What is the best way to bet on horses?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Many expert and professional gamblers will tell you the best way to bet on horse racing is with single bets, on either the win or place markets. Once you combine selections into one bet, the probability of it winning drops, the strike rate falls, and the odds get bigger. While that can lead to bigger wins, it's harder to make a slow, steady profit than by betting singles alone.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Can you bet on a horse to lose?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, it's possible to bet on a horse to lose. This was once the reserve of the bookmaker, but betting exchanges let you bet like one, and many sites now offer the option to back a horse not to win. On an exchange, you lay the horse by offering odds to others who want to back it to win, which differs from a standard bookmaker where the question is simply whether the horse will win the race.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What types of bets can you make on horses?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Beyond backing a horse to win, there are a huge number of options. From combining two selections into a double to predicting the first two home (known as a forecast or exacta), there are dozens of bet types available on horse racing.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"How often does the favourite horse win?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"The favourite wins around 30% of races on average. This is a fluid figure that fluctuates with factors such as the course, the time of year and the going. It's worth investigating more specific favourite-winning statistics on racing stats websites, where you may find courses or conditions at which favourites win more or less often than the general 30% figure, and spot a betting angle.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"What are the best horse racing tips today?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"The best horse racing tips today are the selections receiving the most predictions from OLBG's horse racing tipsters. Free horse racing tips marked with a crown denote the number of experts backing that selection. Experts are OLBG tipsters with high strike rates and current month or 6-month profitability for a particular sport.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"When will horse racing tips for tomorrow be available?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"The free horse racing tips for tomorrow are available to view now. Tipsters begin placing their selections from the afternoon before race day, and tips are added up to around 15 minutes before the scheduled off. A tipster may add a tip early if they think the available value is good and expect it to shorten.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Should I only use free horse racing tips?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"We believe you don't need to pay for selections from subscription services when we have daily free horse racing tips here from OLBG's expert tipsters. Our tipsters compete for generous prize money in our monthly tipster competitions, so they do not need to sell their tips. Each tipster's profit figures covering up to the last 12 months are shown with their racing tips every day, so you can see who's performing well and choose who to follow.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Do you have Lucky 15 horse racing tips?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \"text\": \"Yes, we have daily Lucky 15 horse racing tips, which can be found on our Accumulator Tips list. The selections are the most popular each-way horse racing tips today from the best profit-performing tipsters on OLBG. The daily each-way Lucky 15 tips are available from around 10 am (GMT); if you'd rather use the selections in a Lucky 15 win bet, that's fine too. You can also build your own Lucky 15 using our acca tool to pick from the free horse racing tips on OLBG.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n    \u003C/script>\u003C/div> \n        \u003Cscript>\n            // Wire FAQ card open/close for non-hydrating render() output.\n            (function initFaqCardToggles() {\n                function bind() {\n                    document.querySelectorAll('[data-faq-toggle]').forEach(function (el) {\n                        if (el.getAttribute('data-faq-bound') === '1') return;\n                        el.setAttribute('data-faq-bound', '1');\n                        el.addEventListener('click', function () {\n                            var card = el.closest('[data-faq-card]');\n                            if (!card) return;\n                            var opened = card.classList.toggle('card-opened');\n                            el.setAttribute('aria-expanded', opened ? 'true' : 'false');\n                        });\n                    });\n                }\n                if (document.readyState === 'loading') {\n                    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', bind);\n                } else {\n                    bind();\n                }\n            })();\n        \u003C/script>\n     \u003Cstyle>\n        .dark.is-faq .sct-hdr h3 {\n            color: #fdfdfd;\n        }\n    \u003C/style>\u003Cp>\u003Cbr>\u003C/p>"}]}},mainContentClasses:void 0,pageSchema:"\u003Cscript type='application/ld+json'>{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@graph\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\n      \"@id\": \"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/2\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.olbg.com/betting-tips/Horse_Racing/2\",\n      \"name\": \"Today's Best Horse Racing Tips | Free Predictions\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"@type\": \"OnlineBusiness\",\n        \"name\": \"OLBG\",\n        \"alternateName\": \"Online Betting Guide\",\n        \"legalName\": \"Invendium Ltd\",\n        \"url\": \"https://www.olbg.com/\",\n        \"@id\": \"https://www.olbg.com/#online-business\",\n        \"sameAs\": [\n          \"https://twitter.com/OLBG\",\n          \"https://www.linkedin.com/company/olbg/\",\n          \"https://www.facebook.com/OLBGUK/\",\n          \"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCZ9IVMkBQO28eqbXcearAqw/\",\n          \"https://www.instagram.com/olbg/\",\n          \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OLBG\",\n          \"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q85790088\",\n          \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/olbg-com\",\n          \"https://uk.trustpilot.com/review/www.olbg.com\",\n          \"https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/sports-betting-tips-by-olbg/id557841747\"\n